==================================================
3. YOUR DAILY 4-HOUR STUDY STRUCTURE
==================================================

BLOCK 1: CORE TECHNOLOGY
Duration: 60 minutes

Focus:
- React or Node.js deep dive
- Alternate between React and Node.js each day


BLOCK 2: DSA + JAVASCRIPT
Duration: 60 minutes

Focus:
- Solve 1-2 coding problems
- Analyze time and space complexity
- Practice explaining your approach


BLOCK 3: HANDS-ON CODING
Duration: 90 minutes

Focus:
- Implement features
- Solve practical coding scenarios
- Build or improve your full-stack project


BLOCK 4: INTERVIEW REVISION
Duration: 30 minutes

Focus:
- Answer questions aloud
- Review yesterday's mistakes
- Recall concepts without notes


IMPORTANT RULE:

Don't spend all four hours watching tutorials. At least half your
study time should involve coding or answering questions from memory.


==================================================
4. MINIMUM TARGETS BY NOVEMBER 15
==================================================

[ ] Solve 40-50 carefully selected DSA problems, repeating them until
    you can solve them independently.

[ ] Review 100+ interview questions covering React, Node.js,
    JavaScript, and TypeScript.

[ ] Build and deploy one full-stack project using React, Node.js,
    TypeScript, and a database.

[ ] Complete two system design exercises and explain them aloud.

[ ] Complete three mock interviews.

[ ] Prepare your resume, start applying, and prepare project stories
    for interviews.


PRIORITIZATION RULE:

These are preparation targets, not guarantees of passing interviews.

If time gets tight, reduce optional tooling and advanced topics before
cutting DSA, core React/Node.js preparation, or mock interviews.


