6. THE SENIOR-DEVELOPER RULE
==================================================

For every topic, be able to do four things:

1. EXPLAIN IT
   Describe the concept clearly and accurately.

2. IMPLEMENT IT
   Write working code without relying on tutorials.

3. DISCUSS TRADE-OFFS
   Explain alternatives, limitations, and design decisions.

4. DESCRIBE A PRODUCTION USE CASE
   Explain where and why you would use the concept in a real
   application.

This is what will distinguish a senior candidate from someone who
has simply completed a course.


